Cumbria LRF - Storm Fenella - SITREP 4
Time of report: 14/01/2026 1200

1. SITUATION
Incident status: Active response
River levels on the Derwent and Greta remain high.

2. SITES AND ROUTES
- M6 J40: CLOSED
- QES Kirkby Lonsdale: CLOSED today
- Keswick School: open as rest centre (run by Cumberland Council EP team)
- Glenridding Village Hall: open as rest centre
- Cockermouth School: open as rest centre (run by Cumberland Council EP team)
- West Coast Main Line (Carlisle to Lancaster): no trains running (run by NR)
- Pooley Bridge crossing: closed to all traffic
- A591 at Thirmlere: closed both directions
- Northside Bridge, Workington: closed to all traffic
- A66 Keswick to Penrith: OPEN
- Riverside Community Centre, Carlisle: operating as a rest centre
- Fellside care home: residents evacuated (run by Fellisde Care Ltd)

3. AGENCIES RESPONDING
Environment Agency, Cumbria Constabulary, Keswick MRT, Westmorland and Furness Council

4. NEXT MEETING
SCG at 1600. Dial-in details as previously circulated.

